            "review_title": "Review at Ya! Restaurant",
            "review_text": "David M\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam15 contributions\n0\nBest for casual lunch and peaceful dinner\nJan 2016 • Friends\nMainly have visited for lunch with coworkers of Japanese and\nVietnamese. The lunch menu consists of Japanese dishes and Vietnamese\ndishes. The taste and amount are nice to both Japanese and Vietnamese,\nnot too much but not too less, and the price is the best deal for\nJapanese restaurant. Having kept visiting for a month, I noticed the\nservice has been getting better as the restaurant gets crowded with\ncustomers. On the other hand the dinner time is relatively calm. You\ncan enjoy your favorite alcohol including various Japanese ones and\nstill don't have to worry about budget. I love both lunch and dinner\nthere.\nI only speak Japanese and English but it's not a problem. They have a\nJapanese staff speaking English very well and Vietnamese staffs\nspeaking simple English and Japanese.\nAdditionally, you can enjoy cooking Takoyaki there. As a Japanese, I\nlove enjoying it with my Vietnamese coworkers.\nRead more\nWritten January 6, 2016\nMak O\nThank you David! Yes lunch time is a bit crowded these days but hope you enjoyed! Next time you can also book a seat in separated room!\nWritten January 10, 2016\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
